Title: AROS: name the port and the upstream date in the version
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: The AROS builds called themselves "1.3-dev (local build)" in the title bar and About box, which does not say which upstream state the port is.
Change: On AROS COMMIT is "AROS port, upstream 2026-11-14" (the pinned master 89ea7597); VERSION reads "1.3-dev (AROS port, upstream 2026-11-14)". The package version is 1.3.99.20261114.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only
Verification: build only; shown in the title bar of the release builds
Removal: update with the pin.
---
diff --git a/src/config.h b/src/config.h
index 9f92bbbfc174fef53480d7253c7544095e0e3798..b28358bd3abc0b658b4d8e76ec3593aa618b1a6b 100644
--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -24,7 +24,12 @@
 
 // General information
 #define PACKAGE "LibreSprite"
+#ifdef __AROS__
+  // AROS port of the upstream master of 2026-11-14 (89ea7597)
+  #define COMMIT  "AROS port, upstream 2026-11-14"
+#else
 #define COMMIT  "local build"
+#endif
 #ifndef RELEASE_TAG
     #define VERSION "1.3-dev (" COMMIT ")"
 #else
